RESOLUTION NO. 2026-116
RESOLUTION OF THE BOARD OF SUPERVISORS OF SAN BERNARDINO COUNTY
CALLING A SPECIAL ELECTION AND SUBMITTING MEASURE I, THE SAN BERNARDINO
COUNTY LOCAL TRANSPORTATION IMPROVEMENT PROGRAM, TO THE VOTERS AT THE
NOVEMBER 3, 2026, COUNTYWIDE ELECTION
On Tuesday June 23, 2026, on motion of Supervisor Hagman, duly seconded by Supervisor
Armendarez and carried, the following resolution is adopted by the Board of Supervisors of San
Bernardino County, State of California.
WHEREAS, the State Legislature has enacted the “Local Transportation Authority and Improvement
Act” (“Act”) with certain limited tax authority for which the revenues are to be used for local
transportation purposes, subject to voter approval; and
WHEREAS, pursuant to the Act, the citizens of San Bernardino County first approved the passage of
Measure I in November 1989 and later approved its extension in November 2004, authorizing the San
Bernardino County Transportation Authority (“Authority”) to impose a one-half of one percent retail
transactions and use tax applicable in the incorporated and unincorporated territory of San Bernardino
County for local transportation purposes; and
WHEREAS, Measure I has provided funding for numerous local transportation projects, including
freeways, local roads, major streets, interchanges, the Metrolink commuter train system, public buses,
traffic signals, and more; and
WHEREAS, the imposition of the one-half of one percent retail transactions and use tax is set to
expire in 2040; and
WHEREAS, the Authority and the Board of Supervisors of San Bernardino County are authorized by
the Act to conduct an election for the purpose of submitting a ballot proposition to the voters seeking
authorization to continue to impose the existing one-half of one percent retail transactions and use
tax solely for local transportation purposes; and
WHEREAS, the Authority by Ordinance No. 26-1 adopted June 3, 2026, has requested the Board of
Supervisors of San Bernardino County to call such election; and
WHEREAS, a countywide election will be held on November 3, 2026; and
WHEREAS, if approved by the voters, the continuation of Measure I would not institute a new tax but
would continue the existing one-half of one percent tax for transportation.
NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED by the Board of Supervisors of San Bernardino County that
the proposed Measure I hereinafter set forth in full be submitted to the voters of San Bernardino
County at a special election to be held and conducted on November 3, 2026, said special election to
be consolidated with the other elections to be held on the same date, and that the County Registrar of
Voters be directed to publish such notice as may be required by law for the ballot at the election to be
held countywide on November 3, 2026, and that the Registrar of Voters include in the voter
information handbook San Bernardino County Transportation Authority Ordinance No. 26-1 including
the entire Expenditure Plan and exhibits, and the Measure which shall appear upon the ballot as
follows:
MEASURE I LOCAL TRANSPORTATION IMPROVEMENT PROGRAM
San Bernardino County Road Repair/Traffic Relief Extension
Without raising tax rates, shall an ordinance to fund repairing potholes; keeping local roads in
good condition; completing freeway/highway projects to improve traffic flow/safety, reduce traffic
bottlenecks; upgrading aging bridges/overpasses; creating local jobs; keeping
student/senior/disabled/veteran transit fares low be adopted, extending the ½¢ voter-approved
transportation sales tax, providing approximately $250,000,000 annually until ended by voters,
requiring audits, oversight, spending disclosure, local control?
YES NO
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that the Registrar of Voters is directed to designate the proposed
Measure as Measure I on the November 3, 2026, ballot and that it appear first in order on the local
San Bernardino County ballot before all other local measures.
PASSED AND ADOPTED by the Board of Supervisors of San Bernardino County, State of
California, by the following vote:
AYES: SUPERVISORS: Col. Paul Cook (Ret.), Jesse Armendarez, Dawn Rowe,
Curt Hagman, Joe Baca, Jr.
NOES: SUPERVISORS: None
ABSENT: SUPERVISORS: None
